    // parry window (200 ms) and the stamina costs (attack 10, skills 15-30, dodge 20; no heavy attacks, R-3.1-04) come
    // from spec 12.7 and ActionBindings checks them against StartingValuesM1; every other timing, cooldown, buffer window
    // and cancel rule is a placeholder.
    // TODO(open): does a parry cost stamina? R-3.1-02 says actions cost stamina, spec 12.7 lists no parry cost; 0 for now.
    // mpCost (R-3.1-04): skills only, small, sized to the class's MP pool (ActionBindings checks 1..ClassDef.maxMp);
    // normal attacks, the dodge and the parry cost none.
    // Each phase lasts its ms rounded up to whole ticks (50 ms at 20 Hz). Effects are in ActionEffectDef.json.
    // parryClassPve/Pvp (R-3.3-04, R-3.3-06): none (uncolored), red, yellow, blue or green; only attacks and skills with a
    // strike or projectile may have one. No player action is colored in M1 (PvP is off).

    // Normal attacks (R-3.1-06, R-3.1-10; user decisions 2026-10-26): a chain of 4 hits per class, each a single strike or
    // shot. An attack press from chainFromMs (the start of Active) asks for chainNext, which starts at chainLinkMs (100 ms
    // into Recovery) or at once when pressed later; no press by the end of the hit, any other action, a flinch or a stagger
    // bring the next press back to hit 1. Hit 4 ends the chain: a heavier finisher (longer startup and recovery; its
    // effect deals more damage and poise). Every hit costs StartingValuesM1.normalAttackStaminaCost (spec 12.7) and is
    // cancelled by the dodge from its recovery. Timings are PLACEHOLDERS (balance is deferred).
